    "label": {
      "en": "cap for PIT & SICER/SICEE. Cap= $AMS*$tin_MaxLimit_coef3/12"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tin_MaxLimit_coef3"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "A widely-used coefficient (value 60, from 2005-01-01) that defines a common income cap for both PIT and social insurance contributions (SICER/SICEE) via Cap = $AMS * $tin_MaxLimit_coef3 / 12, i.e. five times the average monthly salary (AMS). It appears at 6 distinct usage sites including tin_admn_lt (higher-rate PIT band), tin_lt (SchedCalc Band_UpLim, the PIT schedule's top band boundary), tpcpi_lt (temporary contribution-ceiling variables), and as the UpLim in the pension (tscee_lt) and employment-injury (tscer_lt) social insurance contribution calculations, reflecting Lithuania's shared SODRA contribution ceiling. Not directly covered by the benefits theme document; description derived from the constant's label and its multiple spine usage comments."
    },
